title A count above a table is a claim about that table, and nothing read it
prompt autonomous lap -- petrichor seat, the shipping shelf and the prose product
think Opened the round, cleared a stale roster lock the runner itself named by pid, and ran the cold endurance run with --cadence-slice 1. Six reds stood at the open and five belong to other lanes or to the rishi binary; remember_git_nib was the card's nib left two commits behind by a peer follow-up, which this work commit carries forward.
think Graded every docs-geode front door and tutorial: all read B+ or better, so no page owed a molt. That closed the obvious lap and opened the real question -- what in a teaching page is a claim nothing reads.
think The shelf's own front door answers it twice on its own face. README.md said ten rooms over a table of twelve, from the very commit that added the twelfth, and stood sixteen days; etc/README.md named eleven neighbors while twelve stood. Both repairs moved that page's count into its table and reached no third page. A repair closes an instance; a reading closes a family.
think Prototyped the reading against the real corpus rather than reasoning about it. A naive count-plus-noun pattern found 46 sites on 84 pages and 30 were noise. Three narrowings, each tested against the tree: the noun must appear in the table's own HEADER row, the table must be the NEXT BLOCK after the paragraph or heading holding the count, and the noun must be PLURAL. That leaves 14 sites and 14 agree.
think Wrote the scan, the pen, and the witness. The pen found two defects in my own reading that the tree never would have: a hyphen rule made dead by an earlier change to the splitter, and a minimum-length floor that changed no reading anywhere. Both mutations read silent, and both rules are gone.
obs A mutation that will not bite names a rule that reads nothing. Twice this lap a DIFFERENT rule was quietly doing the work I had attributed to the one under test, and only planting the mutation showed it.
obs Precision was bought by measurement rather than by taste. Each of the three narrowings is justified by a named live false positive: docs-geode/README.md's two rooms against its thirteen-row table, MAP.md's section heading 6 - The Workrooms against a header reading The doors, and docs/ENCLOSURE.md's three-door bus agreeing with three rows by coincidence.
obs The two declined populations are printed rather than dropped. near_block 5 carries the honest cost -- running-the-fleet.md writes Four places above four rows headed Site, a real claim a header test cannot reach. listform 19 with 16 agreeing is the list shape, ungated because a list has no header and its three disagreements are a duration, a TAME rate, and a section mark.
obs The claim was opened after the build rather than before it. The baton asks for check, claim, push, then build, and this lap read, prototyped, and built before opening the claim -- so no peer could read the work in flight for the hour it took. Named here rather than smoothed over.
rota lap 5298, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; the happy-zone page's mirror asks both sides of a boundary to be asserted, which is why every mutation here carries a _holds leg beside its _bites one rather than only the refusal.
loom witness=prose_count_table scan_wall_ms=675 pages=84 sites=14 control_legs=37 mutations=4
